{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>He does not slander with his tongue</b> — like וַיְרַגֵּל בְּעָבְדְּךָ (2 Samuel 19:28, 'he slandered your servant'). The meaning: to uncover secrets in the manner of spies." "<b>He does not lift up</b> — in the manner of לֹא תִשָּׂא שֵׁם שָׁוְא (Exodus 20:7, 'you shall not lift up a name in vain'). Some say: he did nothing for which his relatives would be shamed."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:17.979118617Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}